DESCRIPTION >
    Flat conversions row-pull (no joins/argMin/window). Faithful 1:1 port of the
    convSql in multiTouchAttribution (api/lib/attribution-engine.js, queryName
    'multitouch_conversions_live'). One row per $conversion, ORDER BY timestamp DESC
    LIMIT 10000. Structural twin of aiplatform_conversions_by_site — same column set
    except the tail: stripe_subscription_id, stripe_event_type (instead of
    browser_name/browser/page_url).
    §2.6 typed-column translation: properties.site_id -> site_id, event -> event_type,
    uuid -> event_id (no `uuid` column; event_id is the Tinybird identifier). conversion_type,
    utm_source/medium/campaign/term, referrer, ai_source, country, device_type, provider,
    attribution_status, stitching_method, ingestion_method, stripe_subscription_id are all
    TYPED columns (events.datasource). `stripe_event_type` is BAG-only (no typed column;
    schema has stripe_subscription_id + stripe_invoice_id, NOT stripe_event_type) ->
    JSONExtractString(properties, 'stripe_event_type'). ''-vs-NULL trap is INERT: the consumer
    collapses via `stripeEventType || null`, so plain JSONExtractString (no nullIf) is faithful.
    MONEY: conversion_value = toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)) (Tinybird dialect)
    == live toFloatOrZero(toString(properties.conversion_value)).
    VALUE-PARITY NOT RUN — founder/orchestrator value-gates vs live HogQL before wiring.

NODE multitouch_conversions_by_site_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        event_id AS uuid,
        distinct_id,
        timestamp,
        conversion_type,
        toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)) AS conversion_value,
        utm_source,
        utm_medium,
        utm_campaign,
        referrer,
        ai_source,
        country,
        device_type,
        utm_term,
        provider,
        attribution_status,
        stitching_method,
        ingestion_method,
        stripe_subscription_id,
        JSONExtractString(properties, 'stripe_event_type') AS stripe_event_type
    FROM events
    WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
      AND event_type = '$conversion'
      AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from, required=True) }}
      AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to, required=True) }}
    ORDER BY timestamp DESC
    LIMIT 10000

TYPE endpoint
